# The format of this file is identical to `.dockerignore`.
# It is used to reduce the size of deployed images to make the process of publishing faster.

# No need to store the pnpm store twice.
.local

# Editor + package-manager caches. These dominate the image (~2.4GB of a 4.1GB
# push) and none of it is runtime state: .vscode-server is the IDE's remote
# server, and the npm/pnpm/node-gyp/tsc caches are rebuilt by the deployment's
# own build step (`pnpm install && pnpm install:playwright && pnpm build`).
# A smaller image pushes faster and spends less time exposed to registry errors.
#
# .cache/ms-playwright IS excluded, despite what an earlier note here claimed.
# It contains only chromium-1223, and locateInBrowsersDir (browserSetup.ts:304)
# matches solely 'chromium_headless_shell-*' — so no code path can reach it.
# The binary the scraper actually launches is chromium_headless_shell-1228 under
# playwright-core/.local-browsers in node_modules, which ships (see below).
.config/.vscode-server
.config/npm
.cache/ms-playwright
.cache/pnpm
.cache/node-gyp
.cache/typescript
.cache/replit
.cache/fontconfig

# NEVER ship local dev state to a deployment.
#
# HISTORY, and the reason this app now stores nothing here: these directories
# held the SQLite database and the exported CSV/zip files. Excluding the
# database from the image was correct — a dev DB carries dev jobs, and the
# deploy's queue processor runs any 'pending' rows at boot, which once replayed
# stale smoke-test jobs against the live endpoint through the operator's proxy
# and got its IP rate-limited before real jobs even started. But it was also
# half the problem: with the file excluded AND a Reserved VM's disk replaced on
# every publish, the deployment started from an empty database every single
# deploy. Order L-3.4g moved storage to PostgreSQL for exactly that reason.
#
# THE SAME HAZARD NOW LIVES IN DATABASE_URL, NOT HERE. If the deployment is
# pointed at the SAME database as the workspace, a dev-created 'pending' job is
# a production job the moment the deployment boots. That is an environment
# setting, which no ignore file can guard — see the L-3.4g ledger's operator
# notes.
#
# data/ is kept excluded because it costs nothing and stops a stale
# ad-library.sqlite from ever riding along again. csv-output/ still holds the
# working files the completion email attaches during a run; downloads are
# regenerated from the database and never read them.
data/
artifacts/api-server/data/
csv-output/
artifacts/api-server/csv-output/

# Do NOT exclude node_modules here. .replitignore is applied when packaging the
# final deployment image (after the build step), so excluding it strips the
# runtime dependencies the build just installed and the server crash-loops with
# ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND at boot.

# Verification sandboxes (scripts/smoke-store-first.mjs, verify-tail-confirm.mjs).
# Same rule as above — the patterns there match those two literal paths only, so
# the throwaway SQLite + CSV these write under a nested data/ would otherwise ship.
artifacts/api-server/.smoke-*
artifacts/api-server/.tail-confirm-check
